FN-MS2S811-1
FISCAL NOTE
Senate Bill 226
Committee: Finance and Taxation General Fund Sponsor: Senator Greg Albritton
Analyst: Peter Grogan Date: 03/04/2026
Senate Bill 226 as introduced would appropriate the following amounts for fiscal year 2026:
1) $387,500,000 from the Public Road and Bridge fund to the Alabama Department of
Transportation;
2) $200,000,000 from the Rebuild Alabama Fund to the Alabama Department of
Transportation;
3) $50,000,000 from the Strategic Energy Infrastructure Development Fund to the State
Industrial Development Authority;
4) $35,137,949 from the Legislative Council Fund to the Legislative Council;
5) $34,000,000 from the American Rescue Plan Act – Small Business Credit Initiative
Fund to the Department of Finance;
6) $22,137,949 from the Refundable Tax Credit Fund to the Legislative Council Fund;
7) $16,000,000 from the Alabama Energy Infrastructure Fund to the State Industrial
Development Authority;
8) $13,000,000 from the Real Property Management Fund to the Legislative Council Fund;
9) $4,100,000 from the State Judicial Administration Fund to the Unified Judicial System;
10)$3,600,000 from the Administrative Office of Courts Federal and Local Funds Fund to
the Unified Judicial System;
11)$2,300,000 from the Court Automation Fund to the Unified Judicial System;
12)$1,268,538 from the Personnel Fund to the State Department;
Page 1

12)$1,268,538 from the Personnel Fund to the State Department;
FN-MS2S811-1
13)$1,000,000 from the Advanced Technology and Data Exchange Fund to the Unified
Judicial System;
14)$1,000,000 from the Vaping and Licensing Enforcement Fund to the Alabama Alcoholic
Beverage Control Board;
15)$1,000,000 from the Consumable Hemp Product Compliance Fund to the Alabama
Alcoholic Beverage Control Board;
16)$588,612 from the Federal Stimulus Fund to the Alabama Medicaid Agency; and
17)$50,000 from the Geological Survey Library Revolving Fund to the Geological Survey.
In addition, this bill would amend Section 3C of Act 2025-251, the Fiscal Year 2025 General
Fund Appropriations Act, to increase the appropriation for the repayment of bonds issued by the
Alabama Federal Aid Highway Finance Authority, Alabama Highway Finance Corporation, the
Alabama Industrial Access Road and Bridge Corporation or the Alabama Highway Authority by
$59,808,596 for a total of $193,564,457.
